          "method_draft": "Use a coordinate/dot-product setup instead of invoking the sine rule directly. Place B at the origin and ray BC on the positive x-axis. Since c = AB = 4 and angle ABC = 30°, set A = (4cos30°, 4sin30°) = (2√3, 2), while C = (a, 0) for some a > 0. Then b = AC. Use the given cos C = √5/3 as the cosine of the angle between vectors CB = (-a, 0) and CA = (2√3 - a, 2). Write the dot-product equation cos C = [CB·CA]/(|CB||CA|). Solve this equation together with b = |CA|; it yields b = 3.",
